### Goal Model Decomposition

The following tables and logical relationships detail the goal model decomposition for the mission of delivering food and retrieving dishes in a hospital setting.

#### Goals Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Enquired Information/Target Condition | Relation | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|------------------------------------------|-----------|----------------|
| G1      | Deliver Food and Retrieve Dishes | Manage the delivery of food and retrieval of dishes in response to requests. | - | Achieve | All food deliveries and dish retrievals are completed successfully. | - | The primary goal encompasses both delivering food and retrieving dishes. |
| G2      | Deliver Food | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room. |ParallelGroupDecomposition:ParallelGroup(G2.1; G2.2) | Perform | - | OR | Food delivery can be done in parallel with other tasks. |
| G3      | Retrieve Dishes | Ensure dirty dishes are retrieved from the room. |ParallelGroupDecomposition:ParallelGroup(G3.1; G3.2) | Perform | - | OR | Dish retrieval can be done in parallel with other tasks. |
| G2.1    | Process Delivery Order | Process each delivery order individually. |SequentialGroupDecomposition:SequentialGroup(G2.1.1; G2.1.2) | Perform | - | AND | Each delivery order must be processed sequentially. |
| G2.1.1  | Deliver Directly | Deliver food directly to the room table. | - | Perform | - | OR | Alternative method of delivery. |
| G2.1.2  | Deliver via Tray | Deliver food via the robot's tray. |SequentialGroupDecomposition:SequentialGroup(G2.1.2.1; G2.1.2.2; G2.1.2.3; G2.1.2.4; G2.1.2.5) | Perform | - | AND | Multiple steps involved in tray delivery. |
| G2.1.2.1 | Check Patient Ability | Query if the patient can retrieve food from the tray. | - | Query | Patient ability to retrieve food | AND | Necessary before proceeding. |
| G2.1.2.2 | Ensure Meal Retrieval | Achieve that the correct meal is retrieved. | - | Achieve | Correct meal retrieved | AND | Ensures the right meal is taken. |
| G2.1.2.3 | Indicate Correct Meal | Perform action to indicate the correct meal for the patient. | - | Perform | - | AND | Action to guide the patient. |
| G2.1.2.4 | Track Retrieval | Track when and where each meal was retrieved. | - | Perform | - | AND | Documentation requirement. |
| G2.1.2.5 | Alert Wrong Meal | Alert if a wrong meal is retrieved. | - | Achieve | Correct meal retrieval | AND | Safety check. |
| G3.1    | Process Dish Retrieval Order | Process each dish retrieval order individually. |SequentialGroupDecomposition:SequentialGroup(G3.1.1; G3.1.2; G3.1.3) | Perform | - | AND | Each dish order must be processed sequentially. |
| G3.1.1  | Robot Retrieve Dishes | Retrieve dishes using the robot. | - | Perform | - | OR | One of several methods. |
| G3.1.2  | Another Robot Retrieve Dishes | Retrieve dishes using another robot. | - | Perform | - | OR | Alternative method. |
| G3.1.3  | Human Retrieve Dishes | Retrieve dishes with human assistance. | - | Perform | - | OR | Another method. |
| G3.2    | Open Door | Open the room door for dish retrieval. |SequentialGroupDecomposition:SequentialGroup(G3.2.1; G3.2.2; G3.2.3) | Perform | - | AND | Multiple steps involved. |
| G3.2.1  | Robot Open Door | Open door using the robot. | - | Perform | - | OR | One of several methods. |
| G3.2.2  | Another Robot Open Door | Open door using another robot. | - | Perform | - | OR | Alternative method. |
| G3.2.3  | Human Open Door | Open door with human assistance. | - | Perform | - | OR | Another method. |

